.TH ISOCMD 1 "November 2026" "Iso Commander 8.0.4" "Iso-Commander Manual"
.ad l
.nh
.SH NAME
isocmd \- manage ISO images, convert disc images and write bootable USB media
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B isocmd
.br
.B isocmd
.RB { \-v | \-\-version }
.br
.B isocmd mount
.RI [ options ] " path ..."
.br
.B isocmd umount
.RI [ options ] " [path ... | all]"
.br
.B isocmd unmount
.RI [ options ] " [path ... | all]"
.br
.B isocmd c2iso
.RI [ options ] " path ..."
.br
.B isocmd w2usb
.RI [ options ] " iso ... device ..."
.SH DESCRIPTION
Iso Commander is a multithreaded, single-binary utility for managing ISO
files, converting disc images to ISO and creating bootable USB media.
Run without arguments to open the interactive menu.
.PP
Mounting, unmounting and USB writing require root privileges.
ISO mount points are located under
.IR /mnt/ISOs/ .
.SH NON-INTERACTIVE COMMANDS
The action must come first, followed by options and then paths.
Options cannot follow positional paths. Unknown actions and options are rejected.
Use a directory prefix (for example,
.IR ./\-image.iso )
for filenames beginning with a hyphen.
.TP
.BR \-v ", " \-\-version
Show the program version and exit.
.TP
.B mount
Mount ISO files or recursively scan directories for ISO files and mount
those found. Requires root.
.TP
.BR umount ", " unmount
Unmount specified ISO mount points. With no paths,
.B all
as the only path, or
.IR /mnt/ISOs ,
scan the immediate subdirectories of the mount directory. Requires root.
.TP
.B c2iso
Convert individual disc images or recursively scan directories for supported
images. Supported extensions are BIN, IMG, CCD, MDF, NRG, CHD, DAA and GBI.
Converted ISO files are saved in the source image directory.
.TP
.B w2usb
Write ISO files to removable USB flash devices. Requires root.
ISO paths must precede device paths, which begin with
.IR /dev/ .
One ISO may be written to multiple devices; otherwise ISO and device counts
must match, with pairs assigned in argument order.
Only whole devices are accepted, not partitions.
See
.B USB WRITING
for requirements and limitations.
.SS Options
.TP
.B \-\-silent
Suppress informational messages, warnings and progress output.
Critical errors are still displayed. The order of options does not affect
silent mode.
.TP
.B \-\-verify
Enable CRC-64 checksum readback verification for
.B w2usb
only. Non-interactive writes use this flag, not the interactive
.B verify_checksum
setting.
.TP
.BI \-d N
Maximum recursion depth for directory scans by
.B mount
and
.BR c2iso .
Depth 0 scans only the specified directories. The default is unlimited;
negative values also select unlimited depth. Rejected by
.BR umount ", " unmount " and " w2usb .
.SH EXIT STATUS
Non-interactive commands return 0 on success and 1 on error or
cancellation, including failure or cancellation of requested verification.
Mount, unmount and conversion commands can return 0 when no eligible
files or mount points are found and no errors occur.
.SH EXAMPLES
.SS Mounting and unmounting
.TP
.B isocmd mount a.iso b.iso
Mount two ISO files.
.TP
.B isocmd mount /path/to/dir
Mount ISOs found in a directory tree.
.TP
.B isocmd mount \-d2 /path/to/dir
Mount ISOs up to recursion depth 2.
.TP
.B isocmd mount \-\-silent a.iso
Mount an ISO with minimal output.
.TP
.B isocmd umount /mnt/ISOs/mountedISO1 /mnt/ISOs/mountedISO2
Unmount two specific mount points.
.TP
.B isocmd umount
Unmount all ISO mount points under /mnt/ISOs.
.TP
.B isocmd umount all
Equivalent to running umount without paths.
.TP
.B isocmd umount \-\-silent
Unmount all ISO mount points with minimal output.
.SS Conversion
.TP
.B isocmd c2iso image.bin
Convert a BIN image to ISO.
.TP
.B isocmd c2iso image.mdf image.nrg
Convert two images to ISO.
.TP
.B isocmd c2iso /path/to/images
Convert supported images in a directory tree.
.TP
.B isocmd c2iso \-d2 /path/to/images
Convert images up to recursion depth 2.
.TP
.B isocmd c2iso \-\-silent /path/to/images
Convert images with minimal output.
.SS USB writing
.TP
.B isocmd w2usb file.iso /dev/sdc
Write one ISO to one device.
.TP
.B isocmd w2usb file.iso /dev/sdc /dev/sdd
Write the same ISO to two devices.
.TP
.B isocmd w2usb a.iso b.iso /dev/sdc /dev/sdd
Write a.iso to sdc and b.iso to sdd.
.TP
.B isocmd w2usb \-\-silent file.iso /dev/sdc
Write an ISO with minimal output.
.TP
.B isocmd w2usb \-\-verify file.iso /dev/sdc
Write an ISO and verify the result.
.SH INTERACTIVE FEATURES
.TP
.B ManageISO
Mount, unmount, delete, move, copy and write ISO files to USB.
.TP
.B Convert2ISO
Convert supported disc images to ISO using ported converters and libchdr.
Conversion is intended for archival use; disc-specific data needed by
emulators may not be preserved.
.TP
.B ImportISO
Create and update the local ISO database, limited to 1 MiB.
.TP
.B Settings
Edit configuration values, themes, display modes and thread limits.
Most settings take effect immediately. The global thread pool limit
requires a restart; automatic database updates are a startup setting.
.TP
.B Exit
Close the interactive application.
.SS List navigation and selection
.TP
.B 1 3 5
Select individual numbered entries.
.TP
.B 1\-3 5 7\-9
Select ranges and individual entries together.
.TP
.B 1\-3 5;
Queue entries as pending selections in supported lists.
.B P
processes pending selections and
.B C
clears them.
.TP
.B 00
Select all entries in the current mount or unmount list.
.TP
.B /
Open the filter prompt.
.TP
.B ~
Toggle full and compact display modes.
.TP
.B *
Toggle filename-only display where supported (not in the unmount list).
.TP
.B R
Refresh the ISO list from folder path history in supported ISO lists.
.TP
.BR PgUp ", " PgDn ", " gN
Navigate to the previous, next or specified page.
.TP
.BR Esc ", " Ctrl+D
Return from the current prompt or list, as applicable.
.TP
.B Ctrl+U
Delete input from the beginning of the line to the cursor.
.SH USB WRITING
.B Warning:
USB writing destroys existing data on the selected devices.
Check device paths carefully before starting a write.
.PP
The non-interactive command checks paths, target devices and capacities
before starting the write jobs. Targets must be removable USB flash
devices with sufficient capacity, no mounted partitions, and no detected
pending writes or cancelled writes still draining.
The interactive device list marks mounted devices as
.B [MOUNTED]
and unmounted devices with pending writes as
.BR [BUSY] .
The number of simultaneous USB write jobs cannot exceed the thread pool size.
.SS Boot compatibility
.TP
.B Windows 10/11
GPT partition layout with FAT32 and NTFS. Supports UEFI boot, not BIOS.
Installation payloads are copied to NTFS without splitting install.wim.
.TP
.B Windows 10/11 PE (WinPE)
GPT partition layout with FAT32. Supports UEFI boot, not BIOS.
.TP
.B Hybrid
Raw sector copy using direct I/O. BIOS and UEFI compatibility depend on
whether the source ISO supports the corresponding USB boot mode.
.PP
Windows versions earlier than 10 are not supported.
The Windows writer requires parted and mkfs.fat, and mkfs.ntfs when an
NTFS partition is needed.
.SS Write modes and verification
Windows and WinPE writes use buffered I/O by default, with controlled
writeback. Set
.B buffered_writes
to off to select direct I/O instead. Raw ISO writes always use direct I/O.
.PP
Optional CRC-64/ECMA-182 verification reads the written data back and checks
it against checksums calculated during writing. Raw writes verify the
written image, including final sector padding; Windows writes verify the
copied file contents. Verification detects accidental corruption, not
image authenticity or bootability.
.PP
Writing and verification have separate progress phases. The final average
write speed excludes verification. Failed or cancelled verification does
not count as verified. The final status is DONE for an unverified write,
PASS for a verified write, FAIL for failure or CXL for cancellation.
.PP
After cancellation, pending writes may continue draining. Wait until the
device is no longer busy before attempting another write or removing it.
.SH FILTERING
Press
.B /
in a list to open the filter prompt. Matching is a plain substring search.
The preview updates as you type; Enter applies the filter.
Esc or Ctrl+D exits the prompt.
.SS Syntax
.TP
.B ;
OR: match entries satisfying any group of terms.
.TP
.B &
AND: match every non-negated term within a group.
.TP
.B !
NOT: at the start of a term, exclude matching entries from the entire query.
.TP
.BR \e; ", " \e& ", " \e! ", " \e\e
Escape a literal semicolon, ampersand, exclamation mark or backslash.
.PP
AND binds more tightly than OR. For example,
.B ping&pong;metal&gear
matches entries containing both ping and pong, or both metal and gear.
A leading negation applies to the whole query:
.B a;b&!t
matches entries containing a or b, but never t.
An exclamation mark elsewhere in a term is literal; use
.B \e!
for a literal leading exclamation mark.
Empty terms are ignored, so
.B a&&b
is equivalent to
.BR a&b .
A backslash before any other character is treated as a normal character.
.SS Case sensitivity
Smart case applies to each term, including negated terms. A term with no
uppercase letters is case-insensitive; a term containing an uppercase
letter is case-sensitive.
.SS Search scope
Each query searches the full, unfiltered list, not the previous results.
Filtering is not limited by pagination. On list refresh, existing matches
are retained and new entries are tested against the active filter.
.PP
With
.B filenames_only
enabled, only filenames are searched, except in the unmount list.
The compact unmount list matches mount-point names without their trailing
~hash suffix; the full unmount list matches complete paths.
.SH CONFIGURATION
The settings editor and the configuration file are documented in
.BR isocmd.conf (5).
.SH FILES
The following user-specific paths are relative to the HOME environment
variable. With sudo, HOME is normally /root.
.TP
.I ~/.config/isocmd/config
Configuration file.
.TP
.I ~/.local/share/isocmd/database/iso_commander_database.txt
ISO database.
.TP
.I ~/.local/share/isocmd/database/iso_commander_path_database.txt
Persistent folder path history.
.TP
.I ~/.local/share/isocmd/database/iso_commander_filter_database.txt
Persistent filter history.
.TP
.I /mnt/ISOs/
ISO mount-point directory.
.TP
.I /tmp/isocmd.lock
Advisory lock file for the interactive application.
